    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.size
      value: 7
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.data[0]
      value: 'I feel I must write down what I have seen for not even the most courageous
        knights would be able to stomach the sight of it.



        King Edward
        ordered our battalion to locate the tomb of Merlin and to seize his staff,
        said to be buried with him. It would give Edward the advantage to finally
        win this long war.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.data[1]
      value: 'We tracked down the tomb to a forest after digging through some old
        texts, the journey was three days on horseback. Eventually we located the
        tomb. Sealed behind a stone inscription which read as follows.



        Merlin
        lies here,

        Ye who would rob,

        Ye who would be damned.



        Damnation
        was not the concern of the men, we opened the tomb and seized the staff from
        the corpse.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.data[2]
      value: 'Skeptical of the legends, one of the men in our battalion was a little
        overzealous and swung the staff, to our surprise a beam of dark emerged and
        shot forth like a shadow clothed thunderbolt.



        The beam eventually
        struck a great ancient vine hanging from a tree which looked several hundred
        years of age.



        The vine fell with a great crash giving flight to
        decades of dust.



        What happened next was the true nightmare.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.data[3]
      value: "A horrible scream rose up from the spot the vine had fallen. In an
        instant a vine-like tentacle shot out and grabbed my fellow soldier holding
        the staff. With the strength of an Ox the man was pulled into the cloud of
        dust, the man\u2019s screaming and the crunching of bones followed."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.data[4]
      value: "This repeated with every single man in the forest, although I was furthest
        back from the creature when it attacked and was able to hide myself.\r\nSuddenly
        I heard a voice. \u201CFools, do you understand what you have done? My last
        act in life was to seal away the spirit of that demon!\u201D I reasoned that
        the voice was probably Merlin himself speaking to me from another plane."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.data[5]
      value: Before I could respond I could hear the staff get crushed and a dark
        shapeless cloud appeared to grow, it looked like the night sky, complete
        with constellations of a great many stars. Once the cloud passed over me
        I found myself to be surrounded on all sides by the night, the ground beneath
        me vanished and before me I saw what appeared to be a map of the world wrapped
        around a sphere, as it spun Europe passed away and I saw a continent I could
        not recognize.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4481454208575651710, guid: 28f576cd3d040ad40a4189793c1ac92a,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: _pageTexts.Array.data[6]
      value: "In an instant vines emerged from europe and wrapped around the blue
        sphere finally stopping, the vines now primarily covered the new continent.
        As that happened The space around me seemed to fold and warp, the motion
        I was subjected to was so unnatural that I could not remain conscious.\n\nWhen
        I awoke I was here, wherever here is\u2026"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
